sentences.text:
Hence, the sentence imposed on the applicant/accused is suspended on the following conditions:-
i) The applicant/accused shall be released on bail on executing a bond for 50,000/-
(Rupees fifty thousand only) with two solvent sureties each for the like sum to the satisfaction of the trial court;
ii) He shall not in any way contact or attempt to contact the victim or family member(s) in any manner;
iii) He shall not commit any offence(s) while on bail;
iv) If the conviction and sentence of the applicant is upheld or even modified, the time during which he is so released shall be excluded in computing the term of his sentence as provided in Section in 430(4) BNSS;
v) It is also made clear that if any of the conditions are violated, the bail shall stand cancelled.
Post on 27/10/2025.

